sec.p:
For each RNA language model, after extracting the embeddings, we apply t-SNE for dimensionality reduction and visualize the 2D embedding space. To quantitatively assess the clustering performance of BiRNA-BERT in comparison to other methods on these tasks, we employ the silhouette coefficient as a measure of clustering quality. Silhouette coefficient is a metric used to evaluate the quality of clustering. It measures how similar a data point is to its own cluster compared to other clusters. The coefficient for a data point i is defined as1\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
