Supplementary Table S4 shows the perplexity and recovery accuracy for BPE-based models (BiRNA-BERT (BPE)), as well as NUC-based models (BIRNA-BERT (NUC), RNA-FM, and RiNALMo). We see that the BPE-based models have significantly lower recovery accuracy compared to the NUC-based models. This is due to the fact that in BPE-based models the vocabulary size is  ~4000 while in NUC-based models the primary vocabulary consists of only four nucleotides along with some additional special characters. The probability of being correct by chance for BPE-based models is \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
