We trained BiRNA-BERT, our 116M parameter model, for two epochs over the same dataset used by RiNALMo29, to ensure consistency and enable a fair comparison. The training was carried out using 8 NVIDIA RTX 3090 GPUs (24GB each), requiring a total of approximately 90 hours. In contrast, RiNALMo, a 600M parameter model, was trained over 14 days (336 hours) on 7 A100 GPUs (80GB each). Given that the training time per step scales approximately linearly with the parameter count30, the expected speed-up from model size alone is \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
