The primary motivation behind training a single model with dual tokenization is memory efficiency. Although having separate BPE and NUC models is viable, we argue that a single model training on both is memory-efficient since only one set of weights needs to be on memory and can process longer sequences and larger batch sizes. Memory efficiency is crucial since the transformer architecture has \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
